{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975784,"nonce":"rz69McBY0PDXHFsGP8xj4Ww3wwY=","title":"LLVM lowerings dereference a possibly-null register where the interpreter does not","message":"HashLink defines several ops on null (`hl_typeof(NULL)` is the void type, a\nvirtual-to-class cast of null is null); the interpreter follows the definition\nand the LLVM lowering dereferences without a test. `GetType` and `SafeCast` from\na virtual are fixed. Still unaudited for the same class:\n\n  - `EnumIndex`/`EnumField`/`SetEnumField`\n  - `CallMethod` (HOBJ), `CallClosure`, `VirtualClosure`\n  - `GetTID` on a type register that could be null\n  - `ArraySize` on null under a non-HARRAY static type\n  - `ToVirtual`/`Ref`/`Unref` on null\n  - `Field` on a virtual, `GetArray`/`SetArray`\n  - every `build_load(..., obj_ptr, ...)` at offset 0\n\nAlso interpreter-side: `Incr`/`Neg`/`Mul` on HUI8/HUI16 wrap at 32 bits where\nHashLink and LLVM wrap at the byte.\n\nThese only surface under AOT because the bodies run once and no parity row\ncompiles a body that runs once. The interpreter is the oracle for each;\n`tools/aot/smoke.sh` is the detector.","files":null}]}